description:
Show the kubeconfig the server runs with, as YAML: the current context alone by default, every context with minified false. Credentials in it are returned as they are.

Example: The current context's kubeconfig: {}

Example: The whole kubeconfig: {"minified":false}

List the events of a namespace, or of the whole cluster when namespace is omitted: warnings, errors and state changes, each with the object it is about. Narrow with fieldSelector, e.g. type=Warning or involvedObject.name=<pod>.

Example: Warnings in a namespace: {"fieldSelector":"type=Warning","namespace":"payments"}

Example: Events about one pod: {"fieldSelector":"involvedObject.name=api-7d9f8b6c4-x2kqz","namespace":"payments"}

Read the system logs of a node through the kubelet: a service such as kubelet, or a log file under /var/log. The last 100 lines by default; tail 0 returns everything.

Example: Kubelet logs of a node: {"name":"worker-1","source":"kubelet"}

Example: A log file on a node: {"name":"worker-1","source":"/var/log/kube-proxy.log","tail":50}

Show the CPU and memory consumption of the nodes as recorded by the Metrics Server: every node, one node with name, or the nodes matching labelSelector.

Example: CPU and memory of every node: {}

Example: Of the worker nodes: {"labelSelector":"node-role.kubernetes.io/worker="}

List the pods of a namespace, or of the whole cluster when namespace is omitted, with their status, restarts and age. Narrow with labelSelector or fieldSelector; pods_get shows one pod in full.

Example: Pods of a namespace: {"namespace":"payments"}

Example: Pods that are not running, cluster-wide: {"fieldSelector":"status.phase!=Running"}

Read the logs of a pod, or of one of its containers: the last 100 lines by default, and with previous the logs of the container that crashed before the last restart.

Example: Last 200 lines of a pod: {"name":"api-7d9f8b6c4-x2kqz","namespace":"payments","tail":200}

Example: Why a container crashed: {"name":"api-7d9f8b6c4-x2kqz","namespace":"payments","previous":true}

Show the CPU and memory consumption of pods as recorded by the Kubernetes Metrics Server: one pod, the pods of a namespace, or every pod of the cluster when namespace is omitted

Example: CPU and memory of every pod: {}

Example: Of the pods of one namespace: {"namespace":"payments"}

Create or update a Kubernetes resource via Server-Side Apply. The manifest is the complete desired state: any field this tool previously set and the new manifest omits is removed. To edit an existing resource, fetch it with resources_get, modify it, then re-apply the full resource.
(common apiVersion and kind include: v1 Pod, v1 Service, v1 Node, apps/v1 Deployment, networking.k8s.io/v1 Ingress, route.openshift.io/v1 Route)

Example: Create a ConfigMap: {"resource":"apiVersion: v1\\nkind: ConfigMap\\nmetadata:\\n  name: settings\\n  namespace: payments\\ndata:\\n  mode: fast\\n"}

List the objects of any kind by apiVersion and kind, in one namespace or, when namespace is omitted, across the cluster, with their names and status columns. Narrow with labelSelector or fieldSelector. (common apiVersion and kind include: v1 Pod, v1 Service, v1 Node, apps/v1 Deployment, networking.k8s.io/v1 Ingress, route.openshift.io/v1 Route)

Example: Deployments of a namespace: {"apiVersion":"apps/v1","kind":"Deployment","namespace":"payments"}

Example: Every Ingress in the cluster: {"apiVersion":"networking.k8s.io/v1","kind":"Ingress"}

Show the replica count of a Deployment, StatefulSet or ReplicaSet, or set it when replicas is given.

Example: Current replicas of a Deployment: {"apiVersion":"apps/v1","kind":"Deployment","name":"api","namespace":"payments"}

Example: Scale a Deployment to three: {"apiVersion":"apps/v1","kind":"Deployment","name":"api","namespace":"payments","replicas":3}
